      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks! This brings the Elan fpinfo handling on par with that of FPC. See [the same function in fpc_private.c](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/driver/fingerprint/fpc/bep/fpc_private.c;l\u003d233-246;drc\u003d611356d2e1fd6e221aa01d32fe50dad6974c5d75).\n\nWe might want to revise this behavior in the future to not just abort here, since one of the functions of this host interface is to transport the `errors` bit field.\n\nThis also explains why I sometimes would see uninitialized garbage in the sensor ID field, when I would run the fpinfo command on buccaneer devices.",
